; perf-gate kernel: :f64-hinted sum over an f64 vector via the numloop JIT's
; vector slot class. The vector is loop-INVARIANT, so the kind guard, base
; pointer and length hoist to loop entry and the body is a bounds check plus
; an indexed load.
;
; n is 200k and stays there: 200k doubles = 1.6MB, which is L2/L3-resident.
; Do NOT scale it up chasing a longer runtime — gate-mat was tripping this
; gate for exactly that reason (a working set in shared L3 times the runner's
; neighbours, not the kernel). Reps carry the duration instead.
; Prints a checksum so a wrong answer fails the gate too.
(def vsum (v :vec i :int n :int acc :f64)
  (if (< i n) (vsum v (+ i 1) n (+ acc (vec-ref v i))) acc))
(= n 200000)
(= v (vec n 0.5))
(= acc 0.0)
(each r (range 0 800)
  (= acc (+ acc (vsum v 0 n 0.0))))
(prn acc)
